## Findings — store 370, worst first

**1. Enclosed, unlabeled lobby room shipped walkable — PDF x 575–633, y 664–734 (~18 m², 772 cells)**

- *Evidence.* Crop `r2c1` / 8× lobby zoom: the front-lobby strip is divided by a drawn partition at **x = 575.1 (y 688.7→733.7)** into the Business Center (already excluded) and a second room to its east, bounded north by the peaked partition `(570.9,684.6)-(593.3,664.6)-(609.5,664.0)-(629.5,683.4)` (PDF drawing #240, same 0.924 stroke class as the Business Center's own walls) and east/south by the store outline. That room was **green**.
- *Why nothing caught it.* No product label lives there, so net 1 was silent; the guide has no floor paint, so net 2 was silent; it isn't a culled pocket, so it never appeared in the top-ten stats. It was reachable **only through a one-cell leak at (630, 682)**: the drawn wall stub ends at x = 632.8, ~0.9 pt short of the outline corner at (633.68, 683.2). An erosion test is decisive — at a **0.3 m** throat those 772 cells split off the 49 674-cell sales floor, and they were the *only* such region in the store.
- *Truth.* Not walkable — same lease/office class as the Business Center beside it and the two restrooms. No door swing, no label, no fixture (every real door in this PDF is drawn as a dashed bowtie swing; there is none here).
- *Fix applied.* `exclusions.json` poly `[[575,740],[575,689],[571,685],[593.5,665],[609.5,664.5],[630,684],[650,684],[650,740]]` — traced to the drawn walls so the genuine exit-approach wedge east of the peak's right leg stays open, and extended to take the exit-threshold notch (x 634–648, y 726–736) that only this room fed, so no orphan pocket is created.

**2. `walk_truth` `must` [600, 700] "exit vestibule east of the Business Center" was inside that room**

- *Evidence.* Probe: the point sits at the centre of the sealed room, not in any vestibule — the exit vestibule is outside the storefront diagonal `(633.68,683.2)–(673.55,642.56)`. This is the pass-4 failure mode exactly: the authored truth point ratified the defect and would have blocked the fix.
- *Fix applied.* Replaced with **[600, 650]** — the real lobby corridor *north* of the peaked partitions, the walk-out path from the checkstand front alley to the Exit doors. Plus new `must_not` **[600, 705]** inside the sealed room: that point alone would have caught finding 1.

**3. Missing `must_not` for the men's restroom interior — PDF x 363–398, y 658–734**

- *Evidence.* Both lobby restrooms are enclosed rooms; only the women's (icon box 403.8–425.7) had a point at (415, 690). The men's room (icon box 369–391) is sealed only by the boundary-trace notch and had no regression lock.
- *Fix applied.* `must_not` **[378, 700]**.

